// [draft]
=== curtains ===
Well, well, well! On my children's lives, your curtains are nicer than mine. #samira #smile
But the chairs aren't in a line, the cups are bone dry, and you… where's your eyeliner, girl? #samira
[[Khalto]] Samira, did you come for a coffee or for an inspection? #salma
Both, sweetheart. I never do just one thing. #samira #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== sweets_case ===
What a lovely sweets case! Perfect for knafeh… and for important guests too. #samira
Important guests? #salma #thinking
Hani, our neighbour's son, the pharmacist. Pure coincidence, he's coming for coffee tomorrow. #samira #smile
Khalto, I spent seven years in marketing. I know a planned coincidence when I see one. #salma
On my children's lives, it's a coincidence! And if it isn't, it will be, tomorrow at five. #samira
Tomorrow at five… I'll bring my chair and watch. #abu_fadi #smile
-> END

// [draft] The choice c2_groom, saved under this knot: chose("basil_pots") is "polite" or "honest".
=== basil_pots ===
Good evening… I'm Hani. Your aunt Samira said that… well… the basil looks nice in the window. #hani
My Teta grew it in the very same spot. Do you like basil? #salma #smile
I do. And I like that the café is close to the pharmacy… I mean, the café is nice too. #hani
* [“Lovely to meet you, Hani. The café is open to you any time.” #polite]
    Thank you. I'll come, for sure… your coffee beats night-shift coffee. #hani #smile
* [“Honestly, Hani? I'm not ready to get married right now. The café is everything to me.” #honest]
    Thank God… I mean, I understand. I only came for your aunt's sake, too. #hani #smile
- -> END

// [draft]
=== wall_photos ===
Wait, wait… that's me! The girl with the braids, that's me! #samira #surprised
And that's my mother, God rest her, and that's your Teta holding my hand. 1974. #samira
Oh, Khalto, you were tiny… and quiet! #salma #smile
Quiet because your Teta popped a [[ma'amoul]] in my mouth. That's how she kept me quiet. #samira #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== tablecloths ===
Salma, a question… does the café stay open late? I'm on night shifts at the pharmacy until dawn. #hani
Did you hear that? He wants to come at night to see you! This one's serious. #samira #smile
No, no… I mean the coffee. After two in the morning, there's nowhere to get a cup. #hani #surprised
You know, you're the second person to ask me that this week. A doctor from the hospital asked the same thing. #salma
A doctor? Forget the doctor! Focus, Salma, focus. #samira
-> END

// [draft]
=== eid_corner ===
The [[ma'amoul]] moulds! The round one's for dates, the long one's for walnuts, and the domed one's for pistachios. #samira #surprised
The last Eid we made ma'amoul here, you and Lana were this big, fighting over the moulds. #samira
I remember the flour… and I remember Lana stealing walnuts off the tray. #salma #smile
And you stole the dates. You both take after your Khalto Samira. #samira #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_lead ===
This was my mother's mould. She'd tap it on the table in time with the song, beat after beat, and never missed once. #samira
And I'd sit under the table, counting the beats… and eating. #samira #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_intro ===
Come on, neighbours, Eid is tomorrow! With the song: tap the mould, turn it out on the tray. #samira_mother_1974
And whoever loses the beat makes coffee for the whole street! #teta_young #smile
Samira, sweetie, the pistachios are for the ma'amoul, not for your mouth! #samira_mother_1974
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_perfect ===
Look at that! Lined up like prayer beads. That's how ma'amoul should be, or not at all. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_ok ===
Never mind the shape, they all taste the same… ask Samira, she's eaten three. #samira_mother_1974 #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_outro ===
When will you have children to fill this café, Um Khalil? #samira_mother_1974
When God wills. Until that day, Samira is my daughter. #teta_young
Samira grew up half in the café. Every Eid, her mould was waiting for her on the table. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m2_return ===
Look at me, crying over ma'amoul! It's the flour in my eyes, nothing else. #samira #sad
This Eid, we'll make ma'amoul here, Khalto. Together. #salma #smile
Deal. I'll bring the moulds… and the groom. #samira #smile
-> END
